psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "\dn"
2. List all tables in every schema:

psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "\dt *.*"
3. Check row counts for key tables:

psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "
SELECT schemaname, tablename, 
       (xpath('/row/cnt/text()', query_to_xml('SELECT COUNT(*) AS cnt FROM '||schemaname||'.'||tablename, false, true, '')))[1]::text::int AS row_count
FROM pg_tables
WHERE schemaname NOT IN ('pg_catalog','information_schema')
ORDER BY schemaname, tablename;
"
4. Check the sra schema specifically:

psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "SELECT * FROM sra.v_queue_kpis;"
5. Check what src tables exist (fact builder reads these):

psql "$DATABASE_URL" -c "\dt src.*"
